The '''[[Forward Progressive Party]]''' was formed on 26 March 2026 when approximately 60 per cent of the [[Forward Party of Burawa|Forward Party]]'s parliamentary caucus defected following [[Marik Sahamin]]'s announcement of his candidacy in the [[2026 Burawi snap leadership election|snap leadership election]]. The breakaway faction, led by [[Mahad Allaale]], cited ideological opposition to Sahamin's leadership and alignment with the progressive platform of [[Muna Xasan]] of the [[Party for Equitable Progress]], whom the Forward Progressive Party formally endorsed in the leadership race.

The split represented the culmination of tensions within the Forward Party that had intensified following Sahamin's removal as party leader in February 2026. Allaale and other progressive members favoured a reformist identity distinct from Sahamin's personal political brand. Following the split, the Forward Progressive Party became the larger of the two Forward-aligned factions in Parliament, commanding 77 Senate seats and 60 Lower House seats.

=== National Party of Burawa ===

{{main|National Party of Burawa}}

